WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Challenge from the Past
Terrifying Zera the Mant

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:37.910
Good morning, Grandpa.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:39.210
Good morning.

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:42.640
You're always such a cutie, Anzu.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.600
What's he talking about?

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:45.580
Where's Yugi?

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.130
Hey, Yugi!

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:49.250
Anzu is here!

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:51.930
Okay!  I'm coming right down!

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.190
That looks good on you, partner.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:03.630
Really?  Isn't it too flashy?

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.200
I think it's too ordinary.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.650
Maybe wear silver jewelry on your arms.

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:09.610
What?

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.310
That won't look good on me.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:16.170
Anzu is waiting for you.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.120
Show her how cool you are.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:20.250
What are you talking about?

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:24.620
Were you talking to someone?

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:27.400
Umm, no...

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:28.690
I'm heading out!

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:32.750
I can tell that Anzu is attracted to you.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:33.660
What?

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:35.670
Don't tease me!

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.390
Yugi?

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:39.980
Good morning, Yugi.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:41.540
Anzu, thanks for waiting.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:43.180
Is that a chain?

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:50.060
This creates a special bond between me and my other self, and it'll never break now.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.920
Yugi and the other Yugi.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:57.590
They're like two sides of Yugi's soul.

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:02.110
I met the other Yugi in Duelist Kingdom.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:08.200
I haven't told anyone, but when I'm dueling, I'm not my usual self.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:15.150
I switch places with my other self that lives inside my heart, and he duels.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:21.510
Yugi says his other soul is inside the Millennium Puzzle.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:23.690
What's wrong, Anzu?

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.350
It's nothing.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.080
Let's go to school.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:28.490
Okay.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:30.600
I'm going, Grandpa.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.350
Have a good day!

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.860
Is he okay?

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.200
What do you mean?

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:39.310
He's talking to himself a lot lately.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:42.970
Kids have a lot to deal with at their age.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:44.870
I was the same way.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:46.770
That's why I'm worried.

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:47.670
What!

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.920
Yugi, are you free this Sunday?

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:58.450
Why?

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:04.970
Nothing special, but if you're free, why don't we do something together?

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:08.920
Well, Yugi?

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:12.230
Yugi?

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.450
What are you doing?

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:17.170
He says he'll tell my fortune.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:20.100
You're such a kid.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.710
You're wearing an impressive accessory.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:29.880
Really?

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.890
May I see it?

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:34.110
No, you can't.

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:35.680
It's very important to me.

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:37.600
Only for a moment.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:38.490
But...

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:46.670
I've traveled around the world and seen every treasure, so I may be able to identify what that is.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:49.490
So...

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.940
Only for a moment.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.540
This is incredible.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:01.980
It's full of history.

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:12.280
Are you okay, Yugi?

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:14.730
Anzu, go to school without me!

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:15.530
I'll catch him!

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:17.460
I'll get everyone!

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.480
He wants me to follow him?

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:38.990
Fine!

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.060
Hey, Anzu.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:51.760
Good morning.

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:53.160
Bakura!

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.000
Yugi's Puzzle was stolen!

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:56.430
Where?

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:57.810
Over there!

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:00.280
I have to tell the others!

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:03.150
I'll look for Yugi.

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:04.110
Thanks!

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.110
Stolen?

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.800
How could he allow that!

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:19.020
What's this?

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:21.930
The Millennium Ring senses a bad omen.

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:26.860
Millennium Items are memory fragments that will eventually come together.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:32.200
I need Yugi Muto to still be the owner of Millennium Puzzle.

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:36.880
Whoever tries to harm him is my enemy.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.020
Is anyone here?

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:32.540
Give my Millennium Puzzle back!

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:37.270
Yugi Muto.

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:41.750
The Millennium Puzzle!

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:43.520
Do you want it back?

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:46.810
Give me back my Millennium Puzzle!

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:50.460
If you want it back, you have to defeat me in a duel.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:04.860
Who are you?

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:07.530
Why do you want me to duel you?

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:11.070
I don't have to answer your questions.

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:13.470
You have one of two choices.

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:16.480
You either duel me or you don't.

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:21.660
So that's Yugi Muto.

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:27.840
He doesn't look like a guy who could defeat Pegasus and win Duelist Kingdom.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:33.860
Does his power come from the other Yugi hiding inside the Millennium Puzzle?

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:42.000
My goal is to track down the soul inside the Millennium Puzzle and uncover the identity of the other Yugi.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:45.300
If he's who I think he is...

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:50.340
My only option is to duel you to get my Millennium Puzzle back?

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.620
What will you do?

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:55.540
Fine.  But you better keep your promise!

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:56.570
Yes.

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:01.550
My other self, can you hear me?

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:02.680
Yugi...

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:07.310
Good.  I can bring you out even from this distance.

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:08.490
No.

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:11.490
You have to fight this duel on your own!

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.400
But why?

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.170
I have a bad feeling.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:20.000
I feel like someone is watching me.

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:23.850
So you can't help me like you usually do?

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:24.840
No.

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:25.950
I understand.

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:31.140
I'll fight for you and get the Millennium Puzzle back!

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:32.780
I'm counting on you, partner.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.960
Let's begin the duel.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:01.640
Yugi, you go first.

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.920
I place Celtic Guardian in attack position.

00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:35.310
I end my turn.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:38.040
I place a monster in defense position.

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:40.240
I end my turn.

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:44.300
I think I've heard his voice before.

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:47.160
What's wrong?

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:48.890
It's your turn.

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:54.800
Celtic Guardian attacks the monster in defense position!

00:10:55.800 --> 00:11:00.200
Cyber Jar flips faceup when it's attacked.

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:02.960
Cyber Jar's effect activates.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:04.570
What?

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:10.950
When this card flips over, all monsters on the field are destroyed.

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:16.190
Then we both reveal the top five cards in our decks.

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:22.940
Any Level 4-or-below monster cards among them are placed on the field in any battle position you like.

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:24.990
Silver Fang in defense position!

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:37.870
Mechanicalchaser, Ground Attacker Bugroth and Cyber Jar...

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:39.880
His deck is a Machine Deck.

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:41.310
Can it be?

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:44.250
Are you Bandit Keith?

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:47.220
You're Keith!

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:51.620
He looks like a different person, but there's no mistaking his bandanna.

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:57.320
Joey defeated him in Duelist Kingdom, and Pegasus banished him.

00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:06.270
Why are you here?

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:10.710
It's true that this man used to be called Bandit Keith.

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:12.140
This man?

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:15.580
Keith was thrown into the ocean.

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:44.850
Why is he talking about himself in the third person?

00:12:45.230 --> 00:12:46.870
And what does he want with me?

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:49.280
Of course he hates you.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:58.320
If it wasn't for you, he could've once again had wealth and fame as America's #1 duelist.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.950
Goddamn, Yugi!

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:06.490
My turn.

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:09.500
I summon Machine King in attack position.

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:19.110
Machine King gains 100 attack points for every faceup Machine-Type monster on the field.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:21.850
Attack Silver Fang.

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:24.710
Jet Punch!

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:31.750
I end my turn.

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:33.920
My turn!

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:37.130
I place a monster in defense position.

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:43.800
You're acting timid because you're afraid of my Machine army.

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:47.430
I'll scare you even more with my ultra rare card.

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:50.440
Megasonic Eye in attack position.

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:55.910
Machine King's effect raises its attack points by 100.

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:59.570
Machine King, attack the defending monster!

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:09.490
Yugi, I thoroughly destroyed your monster.

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:16.370
Well?  Why don't you bring out your other self, like you did during Duelist Kingdom?

00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:20.300
Keith doesn't know about my other self.

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.220
So how does he know?

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:24.240
Maybe that's not Keith!

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:26.420
What?

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:28.950
Someone stole Yugi's Millennium Puzzle?

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:33.050
It must be someone who's jealous of Yugi's success during Duelist Kingdom!

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:35.580
He may be after Yugi too.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:36.620
Let's go!

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:37.240
Yeah!

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:39.920
Where do you think you're going?

00:14:41.090 --> 00:14:43.360
Class is about to begin!

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:46.320
Yugi Muto suddenly fell ill!

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:49.800
He's calling our names as he gasps for breath!

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:53.730
If we don't go, Yugi may...

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:56.960
I see!

00:14:56.960 --> 00:14:58.940
Hurry up and go!

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.610
Yes, teacher!

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:04.580
Cheer Muto up!

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:06.220
That was easy.

00:15:06.220 --> 00:15:08.700
But it'll be scary if he finds out the truth.

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:10.750
It can't be helped.  It's an emergency.

00:15:11.020 --> 00:15:12.730
The rear end justifies the means.

00:15:12.730 --> 00:15:14.220
That's not how the saying goes.

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:15.400
Then a huge dum-

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:16.620
Don't say it!

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:26.800
Yugi, reach for the Millennium Puzzle.

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:29.420
And call out the soul inside it.

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:32.970
I won't do what you want!

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:34.420
My turn!

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:39.170
Curse of Dragon in attack position.

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:41.930
And Gaia The Fierce Knight!

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:48.120
I fuse Gaia The Fierce Knight and Curse of Dragon.

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:58.900
Its attack points are still equal to Machine King's.

00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:01.630
Gaia the Dragon Champion, attack Mechanicalchaser!

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:05.880
Double Dragon Lance!

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:11.050
Machine King loses 100 attack points!

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.460
My turn.

00:16:15.460 --> 00:16:17.000
I change battle positions.

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:22.560
I switch Megasonic Eye and Ground Attacker Bugroth to defense position.

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:26.660
With my rare card Machine Conversion Factory...

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:31.400
...Machine-Type monsters gain 300 attack and defense points.

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:37.510
Oh no!  Gaia the Dragon Champion will be destroyed!

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:39.370
Go, Machine King.

00:16:39.370 --> 00:16:41.660
Attack Gaia the Dragon Champion.

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:45.950
What's wrong?

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:48.450
Will you lose without doing anything?

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:52.660
Won't that ruin your stature as Duelist Kingdom champion...

00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:56.320
...and the man who defeated Pegasus?

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:59.330
Show your true power, like you usually do!

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:05.630
When my other self is in trouble, he never gives up and calmly analyzes the situation.

00:17:06.110 --> 00:17:10.220
He would find the Machine army's weakness.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:11.340
But...

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:13.670
Summoned Skull.

00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:20.800
I know!

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:24.580
The more precise the machine, the more weaknesses it has!

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:26.220
I'll prove that to you!

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:28.030
My combo attack!

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:29.600
Makiu, the Magical Mist!

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:35.730
What's this mist?

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:47.840
And Summoned Skull in attack position!

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:53.780
Summoned Skull's electric attack powers up when your Machines are wet!

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:57.400
Magic Lightning!

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:03.300
Yeah!  I made a huge comeback!

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:04.550
What?

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:07.830
He duels better than I expected.

00:18:08.260 --> 00:18:14.130
I was only watching him so that he would call out the other soul inside the Millennium Puzzle.

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:16.660
Now I'll do whatever it takes!

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:22.860
My special replica cards will unleash consecutive attacks to force out the other soul!

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:24.430
Is this the place?

00:18:24.430 --> 00:18:25.160
Yeah.

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:32.690
This arrow may point to Yugi's location, Anzu.

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:35.150
But who would put it up?

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:37.130
Hey, look at that.

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:41.680
This doesn't help.

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:44.760
It's your turn.

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:52.750
The spell card Graceful Charity allows me to draw three cards from my deck.

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:55.310
Then I discard two cards from my hand.

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:14.060
The ultra rare card Zera Ritual!

00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:30.780
Zera Ritual lets you summon Zera the Mant by tributing monsters whose Levels total more than 8.

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:32.050
That's right.

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:36.150
Among Fiend-Type monsters, Zera the Mant is a powerful and ferocious card.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:40.300
But there are only three copies in the world!

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:46.330
My grandpa said that not many people have seen it because it's the ultra of the ultra rare cards.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:47.960
No way!

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:55.070
I tribute Ground Attacker Bugroth and Megasonic Eye to summon Zera the Mant.

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:14.620
Even Summoned Skull can't destroy Zera.

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:18.250
Devil's Claw!

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:27.130
There's no way I can destroy that ultra rare card!

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:41.610
This is no ordinary duel.

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:45.340
Someone with shadow powers is behind this.

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:48.490
Yugi, where are you?

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:50.750
Yugi, answer us!

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:51.920
Yugi!

00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:54.360
Yugi...

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:57.200
What's wrong?  Reach out with your hand.

00:20:57.390 --> 00:21:01.680
Reach for the Millennium Puzzle and call for the other one.

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:05.370
I want to know who he is!

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:08.550
Yugi...

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:11.980
Your back is against the wall.

00:21:12.570 --> 00:21:16.650
Where's that invincible Yugi from Duelist Kingdom?

00:21:17.140 --> 00:21:22.020
My other self, I can't get the Millennium Puzzle back unless things change.

00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:26.220
Come out, the other Yugi.

00:21:28.560 --> 00:21:31.560
What should I do?

00:21:35.720 --> 00:21:39.680
The fortuneteller who attacked Yugi is Keith!

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:45.050
As if he's controlled by someone, Keith uses rare cards to assault Yugi.

00:21:45.050 --> 00:21:47.340
But he's acting strange.

00:21:47.340 --> 00:21:49.170
What are you doing?

00:21:49.170 --> 00:21:51.510
You're breaking apart Yugi's Millennium Puzzle!

00:21:51.510 --> 00:21:55.770
Surrounded by fire in the abandoned building, Yugi frantically rebuilds his Puzzle.

00:21:55.770 --> 00:21:57.900
Please escape now!

00:21:58.140 --> 00:22:01.050
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Millennium Puzzle in Pieces

00:22:01.050 --> 00:22:02.620
Duel, standby!

00:22:17.220 --> 00:22:21.730
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:22.530 --> 00:22:27.100
I feel like I've been here

00:22:27.630 --> 00:22:36.750
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:37.070 --> 00:22:48.270
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:55.770
Time passes bit by bit

00:22:56.460 --> 00:23:01.040
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:01.630 --> 00:23:06.150
Will never change

00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:11.420
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:12.080 --> 00:23:16.650
To be who I am

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:21.860
I've kept searching for something

00:23:22.550 --> 00:23:26.570
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:26.570 --> 00:23:29.530
I learned that's the answer

00:23:30.330 --> 00:23:36.610
From now until forever...
